.TH SSHPASS 1 "November 15, 2026" "sshpass 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sshpass \- provide an SSH password non-interactively
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sshpass
.RB [ \-f " file" | \-d " fd" | \-p " password" | \-e ]
.RB [ \-P " prompt" ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.I command
.RI [ argument ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sshpass
runs a command with a dedicated pseudo-terminal and supplies a password when
the command displays a recognised password prompt. It is normally used with
.BR ssh (1),
which ordinarily obtains passwords from a controlling terminal.
.PP
By default, both "Password:" and "password:" are recognised. If no password
source option is given, the password is read from the first line of standard
input.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " password"
Use the supplied command-line password. This is the least secure source because
command-line arguments may be visible to other processes.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Read the password from the first line of
.IR file .
.TP
.BI \-d " fd"
Read the password from the inherited file descriptor
.IR fd .
.TP
.B \-e
Read the password from the
.B SSHPASS
environment variable.
.TP
.BI \-P " prompt"
Recognise only
.I prompt
instead of the normal "Password:" or "password:" prompt.
.TP
.B \-v
Write prompt-detection diagnostics to standard error.
.TP
.B \-h
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-V
Display version information and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
If no sshpass-specific error occurs, the command's exit status is returned.
The following values describe errors detected by sshpass:
.TP
.B 1
Invalid command-line argument.
.TP
.B 2
Conflicting password sources.
.TP
.B 3
General runtime error.
.TP
.B 4
Unrecognised response from the command.
.TP
.B 5
The password prompt appeared again, indicating an incorrect password.
.TP
.B 6
The remote host key is unknown. sshpass exits without accepting it.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
SSHPASS='secret' sshpass -e ssh user@example.com
sshpass -f password.txt rsync -e ssh file user@example.com:/tmp/
.fi
.SH SECURITY
Automating password authentication removes protections provided by interactive
entry. Prefer SSH public-key authentication. For programmatic use, an anonymous
pipe passed with
.B \-d
avoids exposing the password in process arguments or the environment.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
